          "disabled": true,
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Luminous Wonder (inspired by J'Adore by Dior): sunshine,bottled",
            "heading_size": 50,
            "heading_size_mobile": 32,
            "heading_line_height": 1,
            "heading_color": "#121212",
            "heading_margin_bottom": 50,
            "heading_margin_bottom_mobile": 30,
            "column_1_text": "<p>A lot of florals save themselves for cooler weather. Luminous Wonder does its best work in the sun. Inspired by J'Adore, it is a glowing bouquet of ylang-ylang, rose, and jasmine that stays golden instead of tipping into heavy, which is not an easy thing for a floral to pull off once it warms up. It smells like the best part of summer: warm skin, a garden at full tilt, that flash of feeling completely put together.</p>",
            "column_2_text": "<p>This is a best perfume for women who want something unmistakably feminine and celebratory that will not turn cloying by mid-afternoon. It carries beautifully in warm air, so a light hand does the job. Wear it to anything worth putting on a nice dress for, and it will hold right through to the part of the night where someone suggests one more stop.</p>",
            "body_size": 20,
            "body_size_mobile": 14,
            "body_line_height": 1.6,
            "body_color": "#000000",
            "paragraph_spacing": 20,
            "column_gap": 60,
            "column_gap_mobile": 30,
            "max_width": 1000,
            "desktop_width_percent": 100,
            "background_color": "#f9f6f1",
            "padding_top": 60,
            "padding_bottom": 60,
            "padding_horizontal": 40,
            "padding_top_mobile": 40,
            "padding_bottom_mobile": 40,
            "padding_horizontal_mobile": 20
          },
          "blocks": {}
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "ai_gen_block_19f144a_BAgRLn",
        "ai_gen_block_614820f_AUBiD6"
      ],
      "name": "Staggered typography",
      "settings": {}
    },
    "blocks_NgyNz4": {
      "type": "_blocks",
      "blocks": {
        "ai_gen_block_fb81b45_qVFqqX": {
          "type": "ai_gen_block_fb81b45",
          "disabled": true,
          "settings": {
            "desktop_width_percent": 100,
            "max_width": 1200,
            "section_padding": 20,
            "background_color": "#f9f6f1",
            "heading": "<p>Test it on skin, not in your head</p>",
            "heading_size": 50,
            "heading_color": "#000000",
            "heading_spacing": 10,
            "box_color": "#8b1d22",
            "box_radius": 25,
            "box_padding": 40,
            "box_spacing": 10,
            "box_paragraph_1": "<p>Two scents that sound perfect together can turn on you the second your skin warms them up, and two you never would have paired can be the ones that work. So spray one on each wrist, press them together, and give it a solid ten minutes before you judge. The first thirty seconds always smell like the fragrance aisle at Sephora during a Black Friday rush. Let the heart come through before you call it.</p>",
            "box_paragraph_2": "",
            "box_paragraph_3": "",
            "box_text_color": "#ffffff",
            "box_text_size": 22,
            "box_text_line_height": 1.6,
            "paragraph_spacing": 25,
            "subheading": "<p>Where the math starts to add up</p>",
            "subheading_size": 50,
            "subheading_color": "#000000",
            "subheading_spacing": 40,
            "bottom_text": "<p>Here's the catch with layering the way the magazines pitch it. Building a wardrobe of designer bottles at over a hundred bucks each is exactly how the whole thing stays reserved for people with money to torch. Do it with high quality inspired fragrances instead and the math flips. For the price of one designer bottle you can own three or four scents built on the same Swiss- sourced oil, mix them however you want, and land on a combination that's genuinely yours. If a pairing bombs, you're out the price of a couple of drive-thru combos, not a car payment. That freedom to experiment is the whole point, and it's a lot easier to hand yourself at around twenty dollars a bottle than at $150 a pop.</p>",
            "bottom_text_size": 22,
            "bottom_text_color": "#000000",
            "bottom_text_line_height": 1.6
          },
          "blocks": {}
        },
        "ai_gen_block_19f144a_ypgJWf": {
          "type": "ai_gen_block_19f144a",
          "disabled": true,
          "settings": {
            "line_1_text": "How to",
            "line_1_alignment": "left",
            "line_1_offset": 205,
            "line_2_text": "actually wear fragrance",
            "line_2_alignment": "center",
            "line_2_offset": 0,
            "line_3_text": "in the heat",
            "line_3_alignment": "right",
            "line_3_offset": -135,
            "body_text": "<p>A few small moves make a real difference in summer. Moisturize first, because warm skin still needs something to hold onto, and hydrated skin holds scent much longer. Stick to pulse points and go lighter than you would in winter, since the heat is already doing half the projecting for you. And keep the bottle out of direct sun; a windowsill in a heat wave will quietly cook a fragrance and dull it over time.</p><p><br/>The practical win with a Scentspired bestseller is simple. High-quality, Swiss-sourced fragrance oil means the scent really lasts through a long, hot day, and at around $20 a bottle you can keep one in your bag for a festival, one in the car, and one by the door without treating any of them like something breakable. That is the whole spirit of summer. You are supposed to be out living in it, not rationing the good stuff.</p>",
            "line_1_size": 42,
            "line_2_size": 55,
            "line_3_size": 42,
            "body_size": 23,
            "line_2_margin_top": 40,
            "line_3_margin_top": -14,
            "header_spacing": 40,
            "body_max_width": 900,
            "section_padding_top": 60,
            "section_padding_bottom": 60,
            "background_color": "#ffffff",
            "text_color": "#000000"
          },
          "blocks": {}
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "ai_gen_block_fb81b45_qVFqqX",
        "ai_gen_block_19f144a_ypgJWf"
      ],
      "settings": {}
    },
